            "grounding": "measured",
            "failure_scenario": "None remaining: before the fix, a tarball-workspace refusal or usage error exited 1 where the Python original exits 2, so a caller branching on rc==2 would misroute; the parity harness now compares the exact code (EXACT_RC=1) for those cases."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "bashrs-sc1044-false-positive",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "bashrs lint reports 2 errors (SC1044, heredoc end token) on the arithmetic shifts $((1 << 61)) and $((1 << 40)); the bash is valid, and no CI step or make lint-scripts (scripts/*.sh only) lints scripts/tests/. Non-blocking; $((2**61)) would silence it. Found by the antigravity lane, reproduced by the reviewer."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/tests/ci_tools_py_parity_test.sh"
